index 0000000..328248b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Migrating-to-v5-Tags.md
@@ -0,0 +1,62 @@
+## Labels and categories are tags
+
+Kronikol 5.0.0 keeps one list of tags on each feature and on each scenario, where 4.x kept a feature's labels and a scenario's labels and categories. A scenario's tags in the report are its feature's tags, then its own. Every adapter reads its framework's own tagging ([[Tags and Attributes › Tags|Tags-and-Attributes#tags]] lists where each one looks), so a suite whose 4.x report showed no tags can show them on 5.0.0 without a change to its tests.
+
+### What changed
+
+| | 4.x | 5.0.0 |
+|---|---|---|
+| The model | `Feature.Labels`; `Scenario.Labels` and `Scenario.Categories` | `Feature.Tags` and `Scenario.Tags`, each the tags written at that level |
+| Where tags come from | LightBDD's `[Label]` and `[ScenarioCategory]`, Gherkin tags, BDDfy's tags and the tests NDJSON; the xUnit, NUnit, MSTest and TUnit adapters read none | every adapter: xUnit `Category` traits, NUnit `[Category]`, MSTest `[TestCategory]`, TUnit `[Category]`, BDDfy's tags and its test's `Category` traits, LightBDD's `[Label]` and `[ScenarioCategory]`, Gherkin tags (a `Rule:`'s included) and the tests NDJSON |
+| `@category:smoke`, `.WithTags("category:smoke")` | the category `smoke` (on BDDfy, the label `category:smoke`) | the tag `smoke`: the prefix is read and dropped, with no warning |
+| Case | `Smoke` and `smoke` were two categories with a button each, and `@smoke` matched both | one tag, spelled as the report first meets it; only ASCII letters fold, so `Über` and `über` are two |
+| LightBDD's `[HappyPath]` | the label `Happy Path` as well as the flag | the flag only: `Happy Path` is a happy-path name on every lane |
+| The filter box | a Categories row: All, a button per category, Uncategorized and an OR/AND switch | one Tags row: a chip per tag with its count, Happy Path first, Untagged, and an ANY/ALL switch |
+| A feature's tags | a badge and free-text search only | they count for each of the feature's scenarios, in the Tags row and in `@tag` search |
+| `@tag` search | a scenario's own labels and categories | the Tags row's tags, Happy Path included; `@"two words"` for a tag with a space |
+| Scenario element attributes | `data-labels` and `data-categories` | `data-tags`, each tag percent-encoded, joined with commas |
+| Toggle default | `ReportToggleDefaults.CategoryFilterMode` | `ReportToggleDefaults.TagFilterMode` (default `Or`, which the switch shows as ANY) |
+| Retries on the ingest lanes | a `retry N` label for each earlier attempt | one retry badge drawn from the attempt (`retry 2` for a third attempt); an author's own `retry 2` is an ordinary tag |
+| Data files | `labels` and `categories` (`Labels` and `Categories` in YAML and XML) | `tags` (`Tags`, and `<Tags><Tag>` in XML), each level's own; `Specifications.md` prints one `Tags:` line |
+| CTRF | `tags` held the scenario's labels; its categories were in `extra.categories` | `tags` hold the scenario's tags, its feature's first; no `extra.categories` |
+| `kronikol query scenarios` | `--label`; `--json` items carry `labels` and `categories` | `--tag`, with `--label` still taken as the same flag; `--json` items carry `tags`, the feature's first |
+| `kronikol merge` | a merged feature kept the first shard's labels | a merged feature keeps the tags every shard gives it, and a shard's other feature tags move onto that shard's scenarios |
+
+Only the framework's category attribute is read: other xUnit trait keys, such as `[Trait("Produces", "openapi.json")]`, and NUnit or TUnit properties are not tags.
+
+### Code
+
+These members are gone, so code that uses them does not build on 5.0.0:
+
+- `Feature.Labels`: use `Feature.Tags`.
+- `Scenario.Labels` and `Scenario.Categories`: use `Scenario.Tags`, which holds both. Code that built a scenario with labels and categories puts both lists in `Tags`.
+- `ScenarioTags.Classified.Labels` and `.Categories`: `Classified` is `(Tags, Endpoint, IsHappyPath)`.
+- `ReqNRollConstants.CategoryTagPrefix`: a `category:` prefix is read and dropped wherever a tag is read, and `ScenarioTags.CategoryPrefix` names it.
+- `ReportToggleDefaults.CategoryFilterMode`: set `TagFilterMode`.
+- `ReportGenerator.GenerateYamlSpecs`: a second writer of the specifications YAML that nothing in Kronikol called. The run writes `Specifications.yml` as before.
+
+`HappyPathDetection.IsHappyPathTag` also takes `Happy Path`, with its space.
+
+### Data files and tools
+
+- **Kronikol.Tool 5.x reads a 4.x file** (`kronikol query`, `kronikol ctrf` and `kronikol merge`): its labels and categories are its tags, and a feature's labels are the feature's. The `retry N` labels a 4.x ingest generated are left out where the scenario's `attempt` accounts for them. A report Kronikol4J wrote with `labels` and `categories` reads the same way.
+- **A 4.x tool reads a 5.0.0 file as untagged.** This change does not move `formatVersion` (it stays 3), so the file is not refused and its `tags` are skipped as a key the tool does not know: `query scenarios --label` matches nothing, `kronikol ctrf` writes no tags, and `kronikol merge` writes a merged report without them. Read 5.0.0 reports with Kronikol.Tool 5.x.
+- **History does not read tags**, so the history action and `kronikol history` work as before, whichever version of the tool reads the file.
+- **A committed `Specifications.yml`, `.json` or `.xml` changes on the upgrade**: its `Labels` and `Categories` become `Tags` (`tags` in JSON), and a suite that tags its tests through its framework gains tags it did not have.
+- **Your own scripts** that read `labels` or `categories` from `TestRunReport.json` read `tags`, on the feature and on the scenario. A scenario's tags in the report are its feature's, then its own.
+
+### The report
+
+- The Categories row is gone, and with it the classes a custom stylesheet may target: `.category-filters`, `.category-toggle`, `.category-active` and `.cat-mode-toggle`.
+- A link a 4.x report wrote keeps its meaning: `cats=` is read as `tags=`, `catmode=` as the tag mode when the link has no `tagmode=`, and `__uncategorized__` as Untagged. 5.0.0 writes `tags=`, `tagx=` and `tagmode=`, each name percent-encoded ([[Generated Reports › Deep links|Generated-Reports#deep-links-scenario--and-sid-]]).
+
+### What a report shows differently
+
+Besides the tags the adapters now read, 5.0.0 changes what some reports show:
+
+- **ReqNRoll:** a feature's tags are its `Feature:`'s (Reqnroll's `FeatureInfo.Tags`). 4.x read them from the feature's first scenario, which gave that scenario's rule tags to the whole feature and lost a feature tag the scenario repeated.
+- **Gherkin rules:** a `Rule:`'s tags reach its scenarios, on ReqNRoll and on the Cucumber Messages lane, where 4.x dropped a plain rule tag.
+- **NUnit `[TestCase]`:** `[HappyPath]` on a `[TestCase]` method marks its cases, and a fixture whose first captured test is a `[TestCase]` keeps its `[Endpoint]`.
+- **A tag with a comma, a double quote or a space** filters, is found by search and survives a link. 4.x split a tag at a comma, and a quote in one broke a shared link.
+- **A parameterized group** shows the tags all of its rows carry, less its feature's.
+- **The chips' order** no longer depends on the machine's culture: Happy Path first, then by name with ASCII letters folded.
